To ensure the reliability and reproducibility of the reported results, a rigorous statistical validation was performed across 5-fold stratified cross-validation experiments. We applied two complementary statistical tests: the paired t-test to assess the significance of mean performance differences under the assumption of normality, and the non-parametric Wilcoxon signed-rank test to confirm robustness, thereby avoiding reliance on distributional assumptions. Both tests compared each baseline model against the proposed SE-FusionEAOO Ensemble using accuracy and macro-F1 as evaluation metrics. As shown in Table 10, the proposed SE-FusionEAOO Ensemble consistently achieved statistically significant improvements over all single models and intermediate fusion configurations, with \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
